From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:06:12 +0100
Subject: [maglev] Use WithFallback in VisitIntrinsicAsyncFunctionAwait
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce SubgraphBase::WithFallback and use it in
VisitIntrinsicAsyncFunctionAwait so that both the fallback and join
labels are always bound or trimmed even when the fast path aborts after
branching to the fallback path. Also upgrade predecessor-count checks in
MergeIntoLabel, TrimPredecessorsAndBind, and
MergePointInterpreterFrameState::Merge to CHECKs.

Fixed: 580867734
Bug: 558240761
Change-Id: I3be168d60330d5a06a4aba84ed18ccaa33a8ae92
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/v8/v8/+/8741062
Reviewed-by: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Marja Hölttä <marja@chromium.org>
Auto-Submit: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Victor Gomes <victorgomes@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#111756}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y): SubgraphBase::WithFallback is added to this branch's SubgraphBase (which already has GotoOrTrim / TrimPredecessorsAndBind). VisitIntrinsicAsyncFunctionAwait is rewritten with WithFallback using this branch's builder API (BuildLoadTaggedField without NodeType, CreateAsyncResumeTask / BuildInlinedAllocation(task, AllocationType::kYoung) on the graph builder, JSPromise::HasHandlerBit). MaglevSubGraphBuilder::Goto keeps this branch's Merge(builder_, ...) call with the new CHECK_LT in front. The IsSmallFunction helper in the upstream context is unrelated and not added.

